      "result": "## Test Summary\n\nI have completed testing the ThreadHive community forum application against all 18 checklist items. Here's the final summary:\n\n### Results: 12 PASS | 6 FAIL\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n**Working Features (PASS):**\n- User profile management with bio and comma-separated interests\n- Discussion creation with categories, titles, and bodies\n- Reply system with real-time updates\n- Upvote/like functionality with immediate updates\n- Keyword search with clear feedback for no matches\n- Category filtering to show only relevant discussions\n- Most Active list correctly sorted by reply count (89→23→1 replies)\n- Author profile viewing with all required details\n- Data persistence within same session after logout/login\n- Incorrect password rejection with error message\n- Trending discussions showing upvote counts\n- Reply count accuracy (displayed counts match actual replies)\n- Community stats accuracy (892 members, 1,045 threads, 4,823 replies)\n\n**Critical Issues (FAIL):**\n1. **FT-1 - Duplicate Email Validation**: System allows registering multiple accounts with the same email address (testuser2 registered with testuser1's email)\n2. **FT-18 - Session Persistence**: User session is lost after page reload; user must log in again\n3. **CS-14 - Missing Field Validation**: Could not fully test; missing validation for required discussion fields\n4. **CS-22 - Unauthenticated Access**: Could not verify redirect to sign-in when unauthenticated users try to create discussions\n5. **CT-20 - Time Window Description**: Trending and Most Active views don't state the time period used (e.g., \"Last 7 days\")\n\nThe forum has solid core functionality but needs fixes for data validation, session management, and user guidance around popularity metrics.",
